From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Proton-SNR
Date: Sat, 27 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ncrypt: Pass through OAEP padding to BCryptEncrypt.

Wine's bcrypt backend already implements RSA-OAEP (SymCryptRsaOaepEncrypt)
and uses the same BCRYPT_OAEP_PADDING_INFO layout and flag values as
NCrypt, so there is no reason to reject NCRYPT_PAD_OAEP_FLAG here.
Required by SuperNewRoles (RSACng.Encrypt with OaepSHA1), which otherwise
fails with NTE_NOT_SUPPORTED (0x80090029) at plugin load.

---
 dlls/ncrypt/main.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ncrypt/main.c b/dlls/ncrypt/main.c
--- a/dlls/ncrypt/main.c
+++ b/dlls/ncrypt/main.c
@@ -238,9 +238,9 @@ SECURITY_STATUS WINAPI NCryptEncrypt(NCRYPT_KEY_HANDLE key, BYTE *input, DWORD i
         return NTE_BAD_FLAGS;
     }

-    if (flags & NCRYPT_NO_PADDING_FLAG || flags & NCRYPT_PAD_OAEP_FLAG)
+    if (flags & NCRYPT_NO_PADDING_FLAG)
     {
-        FIXME("No padding and oaep padding not supported\n");
+        FIXME("No padding not supported\n");
         return NTE_NOT_SUPPORTED;
     }

